===''[[Disney Mirrorverse]]''===
Within Mirrorverse, Tigger takes on the role of the "Surprising Storybook Scout", having become separated from the rest of his Hundred Acre Woods friends and seeking to reunite the group with his Stellar Magic enhanced bouncing. Tigger is the only Pooh character in the game, and the game was shut down before any other Pooh characters could be added.

=== ''[[Disney Dreamlight Valley]]'' ===
Tigger joined the game in the Wishblossom Ranch expansion. He can be found in Pixie Acres. He lives in his treehouse. Tigger unknowingly overused the Ranch's Wish Magic and caused the Decay. 

==[[Walt Disney Parks and Resorts|Disney Parks]]==
[[File:Tigger Disney parks .jpg|thumb|250px|Tigger posing for a photo at one of the Disney parks.]]
In the Disney theme parks around the world, Tigger is a very common character who usually appears with Pooh or Eeyore, and occasionally Piglet and Rabbit.

Tigger appears in [[The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh (attraction)|The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh]] as an audio-animatronic. Tigger is first seen after the ''Blustery Day'' and ''Honey Tree'' sections and bounces with the riders and eventually introduces the Heffalumps and Woozles scene. In the [[Walt Disney World]] and [[Hong Kong Disneyland]] versions of the attraction, Tigger's voice work is done by the late Paul Winchell while in [[Disneyland]], it's done by Jim Cummings.

===[[Disneyland Resort]]===
Tigger appeared in the [[World of Color]] pre-show as a large puppet with a flashy body system along with [[Lumiere]], [[Sebastian]], [[Genie]], and [[Mike Wazowski]]. Some of the puppets were later used in the [[Paint the Night]] parade at the Disneyland park.

In the [[World of Color#World of Color:Celebrate!|2015 rendition of World of Color]], Tigger made a cameo appearance during the opening sequence, in honor of Walt Disney.

For meet-and-greets, Tigger can be found in [[Critter Country]].

===[[Walt Disney World]]===
In Florida, Tigger can be found in the [[Magic Kingdom]]'s [[Fantasyland (Magic Kingdom)|Fantasyland]], the [[Crystal Palace]] buffet, and the [[United Kingdom Pavilion]] in [[Epcot]] for meet-and-greets.

Tigger's voice can be heard during [[Once Upon a Time (fireworks show)|Once Upon a Time]] at the [[Magic Kingdom]], where he introduces the Heffalumps and Woozles.

In the game show "Win, Lose or Draw" during Disney World Week, Tigger is seen on a sailboat with host Bert Convy.

===[[Tokyo Disney Resort]]===
In [[Pooh's Hunny Hunt]], Tigger bounces along with the audience while singing "[[The Wonderful Thing About Tiggers]]".

In 2010, he hosted the New Year's Day event to celebrate the Year of the Tiger.

===[[Shanghai Disneyland]]===
In Shanghai, Tigger is one of the characters part of [[Garden of the Twelve Friends]], representing the Chinese Zodiac symbol of the tiger. He also appears during [[Mickey's Storybook Express]] and Fantasy Festival. As well, he hosted the Year of the Tiger event in 2022.

